    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d723">

                <pb facs="0844" n="834" xml:id="pg834"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5–2948: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-05-29T12:00:00+09:00">May 29, 1948—noon.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 29—7:32 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>973. Current reports emanating from Ministry National Defense indicate Communists
                    concentrating both sides Tsinpu<anchor n="51" xml:id="d723-f1"/> r[ail-] road
                    near vicinity of Tenghsien. Nationals have moved several divisions from Hsuchou
                    to northern Kiangsu. Thus Communists probably have capability and intention
                    isolating Tsinan. We believe all Americans remaining Tsinan should be advised
                    depart at once unless prepared undergo isolation and possible siege.</p>
                <p>Shanghai should repeat substance of above to heads of interested mission
                    boards.</p>
                <p>Sent Tsingtao 83, Shanghai 432.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d723-f1" n="51" xml:id="d723-f1-content">
                <p>Tientsin–Pukow.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
